// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6078 new: Potential Browser Cache Smuggling Payload Extraction
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6078
// Pull request author: Tetryl12
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Browser Cache Smuggling Payload Extraction
// Sigma ID: 93e79eb5-2aca-4d1d-895d-0f529127e088
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Chris Wright (https://github.com/Tetryl12)
// Date: 2026-06-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027, execution, T1059.001, T1204.004
// Description: Detects a process reading, searching, or extracting content directly out of a web browser's on-
//   disk cache directory (Chromium "Cache_Data", Firefox "cache2\entries", or the
//   legacy/WebView2/Outlook "INetCache"). In the "cache smuggling" / "Living off the Browser"
//   technique, a phishing page (commonly a ClickFix or FileFix lure) serves an executable payload
//   disguised with an "image/jpeg" Content-Type so the browser silently caches it with no download
//   prompt and no Mark-of-the-Web. The victim is then social-engineered into pasting a benign-
//   looking command that carves the payload out of the cache file (often between two marker strings
//   via regex), writes it to a writable/executable location, and runs it. Because no second network
//   request is made, network/proxy controls and download/MotW-based detections are evaded. This rule
//   targets the local extraction step rather than the (invisible) delivery step.
// False positives:
//   - Browser cache maintenance, backup, or DLP/AV tools that read cache contents. Tune via the Image / ParentImage of approved tooling.
//   - Forensic or IR tooling (e.g. cache parsers) run by analysts. Filter on known investigator hosts/accounts.
//   - Developers debugging browser cache behavior with PowerShell.
// References:
//   - https://expel.com/blog/cache-smuggling-when-a-picture-isnt-a-thousand-words/
//   - https://malwaretech.com/2025/10/exif-smuggling.html
//   - https://www.cybermaxx.com/resources/cache-smuggling-the-interesting-download-cradle-provided-by-your-internet-browser/
//   - https://sensepost.com/blog/2023/browsers-cache-smuggling/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/a06ed17260fe996129061bbca888b168c84b03e9/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_browser_cache_smuggling_extraction.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Cache_Data" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\cache2\\entries" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Windows\\INetCache") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-ChildItem" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-Content" or ProcessCommandLine contains "[IO.File]::ReadAllBytes" or ProcessCommandLine contains "[System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ReadAllText" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Select-String" or ProcessCommandLine contains "findstr" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-match" or ProcessCommandLine contains "[regex]" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".Matches(" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Copy-Item" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Move-Item" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Expand-Archive" or ProcessCommandLine contains "FromBase64String" or ProcessCommandLine contains "certutil" or ProcessCommandLine contains "tar " or ProcessCommandLine contains "expand ")) and (not((FolderPath endswith "\\ccleaner.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\ccleaner64.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\bleachbit.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\bleachbit_console.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cleanmgr.exe")))
